\label{thm:min-bis}
Consider $\ensuremath{\mathrm{CM}_n(\boldsymbol{d})}$ satisfying {\rm Assumption~\ref{assumption1}}, and let $k\geq 2$ be an integer.
 Then $w_k(\ensuremath{\mathrm{CM}_n(\boldsymbol{d})})$ exhibits a phase transition around $\eta =1/k$. More precisely, 
 \begin{enumerate}[{\normalfont (i)}]
 \item \label{thm:min-bis-i} If $\eta <1/k$, then  with high probability $w_k(\ensuremath{\mathrm{CM}_n(\boldsymbol{d})})\leq k/2$;
 \item \label{thm:min-bis-ii} If $\eta >1/k$, then there exists $\zeta>0$, such that with high probability $w_k(\ensuremath{\mathrm{CM}_n(\boldsymbol{d})})>\zeta n$.
 \end{enumerate}


